                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1173: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-08T18:00:00-06:00">April 8, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Complete and friendly accord on a recess for 2 months was obtained and an act
                    suspending plenary sessions to give ample time for necessary studies was signed
                    at 4 p.m. this afternoon by both delegations and the members of the Mediation
                    Commission. Press informed. Travel authorization requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
